From c2507fae6202f4924a7ac683d646b7dd9bd329bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:10:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v1 4/4] usb: typec: mux: add Silicon Mitus SM5714 MUIC data
 switch driver
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The SM5714 MUIC contains the analog switch for the USB D+/D- data
lines. In automatic mode it runs BC1.2 charger detection and routes
the data lines itself, which works while the port acts as a USB
device. When the port acts as a host it leaves the data lines open,
so the switch has to be forced onto the USB path manually.

Add a Type-C mode switch driver: it is driven through the connector
graph by the SM5714 Type-C CC detection block. TYPEC_STATE_USB forces
the USB data path (manual mode), while any other state returns the
switch to automatic mode so BC1.2 charger detection keeps working.
Alternate modes are rejected since this switch only routes USB D+/D-.

Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mráz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
